title Caravan ladder reach -- a rung folds into the rung directly below it, and a guard says so
prompt Autonomous loop -- Standfast on reds, then the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, council rota doc by lap index, condense REMEMBER when a set completes, and send each finished increment as its own signed round.
think Standfast first. Walked crux/REDS.md and every archived range: rows 88-95 all closed on metal per the archive header, %96 and %97 closed in the living pin, %81 %84 %90 %95 closed by name. No agent-closable red stood open, so constructive work was free to begin.
think Council rota, lap 535 of the d27 cycle: context/SILO_TECHNIQUE.md, read whole. An idea is truly ours only when we can rebuild it from our own materials -- which is exactly the test this lap applied to a number rather than a source. The meter handed over a total; reading the parts until the shape was ours is what found the drift.
think The newest log named its own next crux in a number: 622 lines a rung, carry 2,574 of 4,000, about two rungs of headroom, and the lift that answers it is the move that already worked once. Lindy-first crux-first agreed -- the harness is the durable thing on this ladder, and the carry is the meter that says whether it is holding.
think Rather than trusting the total, read which bodies made it. 89 duplicated bodies between mind and desist: four real bodies at 197 lines, and 85 identical five-line stubs. That decomposition is the whole lap. Two rungs only write the same stub when they name the same rung below.
think Measured every rung's fold target. Thirty-two rungs fold; thirty-one name a distinct rung below. One collision: desist and mind both fold into forbearing_rung. desist.rye was born as a copy of mind.rye -- which is what makes the parity of every rung beneath it readable -- and it inherited mind's delegations whole, reaching two rungs down and skipping its own neighbor.
think Three moves, in order. Repointed desist's 39 folds to minding_rung, one step down, after asserting all 39 stand pub on mind.rye. Lifted the four remaining copied bodies -- check_mind, check_mind_refusals, check_forbear_measure, check_forbear_wire -- into caravan/ladder_checks.rye, following the precedent check_allay_measure already set: the inventing rung keeps its own body where its chain ends, every rung above it shares the harness body whose tail re-enters the rung.
think Then the prevention, which is the part that outlives the fix. The one-step rule was true everywhere and written nowhere a machine could read it, so it became tools/fixtures/caravan_ladder_reach_scan.sh -- a rung folds into at most one rung, and no rung is folded into by two -- and a sixth claim on the copy meter.
obs The fix is worth less than the rule it taught. A rung born as a copy of the rung beneath it inherits that rung's reach, not its own; nothing in the tree said so, and the cost showed up as a number in a different guard entirely. Booked REDS %98 with the closure, since a drift that shipped is a red whatever else it teaches.
obs The strongest proof available was the tree itself. Beyond a three-rung PASS corpus and a planted skip corpus, the guard ran against the living ladder as it stood this morning and named the real drift by name -- forbearing_rung is folded into by more than one rung: desist mind. A guard proven on the very fault it was written for cannot be a habit wearing a check's clothes.
obs Fold A held at 679 exactly through the repoint, which is the honest signal that nothing was lost: repointing changes which rung a fold names, never how many folds stand. Fold B climbed 484 to 492 -- the eight new stubs, four each in mind and desist -- and the carry fell 372 lines net.
obs Docs moved in the same commit rather than a later sweep. The README's harness paragraph now states the one-step rule and cites the scan; both the meter witness's header and the scan's header carried a standing of 1,952 that had not been true for two rungs, so each names 2,202 now. A doc describing behavior the code no longer has is a stale claim wearing documentation's clothes.
obs One limit named rather than rounded away: the remaining 2,202 lines are mostly irreducible. A lifted check costs each rung five lines of stub, byte-identical across rungs by design since @This() resolves per rung, and the meter counts every one past the first as carried. The carry can fall further only by lifting bodies that have not been lifted -- never to zero.
loom witness=caravan_ladder_copy carry_lines=2202 prior=2574 fold_a=679 fold_b=492 folding_rungs=32 modules=95 checks=1491
loom witness=caravan_suite rungs=89 cold_tree=true result=GREEN
file caravan/desist.rye 39 folds repointed from forbearing_rung to minding_rung, one step down, and four copied bodies replaced by harness stubs
file caravan/mind.rye the same four bodies replaced by harness stubs, so one body now serves both rungs
file caravan/ladder_checks.rye the four lifted bodies, each taking the rung as a comptime parameter and re-entering it at the tail
file tools/fixtures/caravan_ladder_reach_scan.sh the new guard -- a rung folds into at most one rung, and no rung is folded into by two
file tools/fixtures/caravan_ladder_reach_corpus/ three rungs, each folding into the one beneath it, small enough to read
file tools/fixtures/caravan_ladder_reach_skip_corpus/ the planted drift -- a top rung reaching past its neighbor, refused as reason=shared_target
file tools/caravan_ladder_copy_witness.rish fold C claim, the fourth RED path, and the standing corrected to 2,202
file tools/fixtures/caravan_ladder_copy_scan.sh header synced to the carry it now measures
file caravan/README.md the one-step rule stated where the harness is introduced, citing the scan that holds it
file crux/REDS.md REDS %98 booked and closed -- root, three fixes, and the guard proven on the living fault
file crux/CAIRNS.md walk-back nib ae3bc5bee3 recorded before the card condense
file crux/REMEMBER.md the correspondence arc folded to one pointer, Now refilled with this round; 47,618 bytes to 32,484
recommend keep-going the ladder's shape is guarded now as well as measured, and the meter names the next crux the same way it named this one: 2,202 lines standing, most of them the irreducible five-line stub a lifted check costs each rung. The nearer constructive door is where the desist rung's own recommend pointed before the meter interrupted -- what an operator does with a wall once it stands, which is where the arc leaves the plan and reaches a person.
